From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FirebirdTA01 <FirebirdTA01@aol.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 17:39:25 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Reject SPUDLL shared links instead of silently linking an ordinary executable.

The SPU linker has no shared-library support. GCC previously consumed -shared
without forwarding it, then selected ordinary startup and libraries. Diagnose
the unsupported mode in LINK_SPEC, including links that suppress startup or
default libraries. Compile-only PIC and backend relocation checks are unchanged.

(Ported to GCC 16 from patches/spu/gcc-9.5.0/0007-spu-reject-unsupported-shared-links.patch.)
---
 gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h b/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h
index ca17b0bdd5b..9a5b3585de3 100644
--- a/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h
+++ b/gcc/config/spu/spu-elf.h
@@ -76,6 +76,7 @@
 /* -dT is a default script: an explicit -T (including a forwarded
    -Wl,-T) wins regardless of the order in which the driver emits it.  */
 #define LINK_SPEC \
+  "%{shared:%eSPUDLL shared links are not supported by this toolchain} " \
   "%{mspurs-task:%{mspurs-job|mspurs-job-initialize:%econflicting SPURS modes}} " \
   "%{mspurs-job:%{mspurs-job-initialize:%econflicting SPURS modes}} " \
   "%{mspurs-task|mspurs-job|mspurs-job-initialize:" \
